DDL – Data Definition Language - (CREATE, ALTER, DELETE):
---------------------------------------------------------

CREATE: to create new database objects
--------------------------------------
    CREATE TABLE <table_name> (
    Col1 <data_type> <constraint>,
    Col2 <data_type> <constraint>,
    Col3 <data_type> <constraint>
    );

e.g:   CREATE TABLE persons (
        Id INT NOT NULL,
        Person_name VARSHACR(50) NOT NULL,
        Birth_date DATE,
        Phone VARCHAR(15)
        CONSTRAINT pk_primary PRIMARY KEY
        );

ALTER: change table structure (add or remove columns, change data types)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ALTER TABLE persons 
    ADD email VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL;

    ALTER TABLE persons
    DROP COLUMN phone;

DROP:  drop entire database object:
-----------------------------------
      DROP TABLE <table_name>;
      DROP TABLE persons;
